# S11.2-R15.14.1 freeze provenance diagnosis — 2026-09-27

## Observed failure

The source-level R15.15 preflight returned
`S11_2_FREEZE_PROVENANCE_RED`. It stopped before every runtime boundary.
The immutable R15.14 tag target is correct, but its annotation satisfies 22
of 29 exact controller bindings.

## Root cause

The tag annotation was manually assembled with five shortened artifact-key
aliases and omitted two runtime-contract bindings. The controller intentionally
uses exact full-line matching, so aliases cannot satisfy canonical names.
This is `IMMUTABLE_FREEZE_CANONICAL_KEY_DRIFT`, not a runtime or product
failure.

## Safe correction

Preserve the old tag unchanged. Bind the minimally changed controller to a
new tag and use one versioned generator/verifier for the exact ordered 29-key
set. Tests prove 29/29 GREEN; 28/29, alias substitution, duplicate key, wrong
artifact hash, wrong commit, wrong tree and the historical annotation all
fail closed.

The final tag values are calculated only after the merge commit exists. No
tag force-update, runtime retry, server access or evidence mutation is part of
this correction.
